---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { amcShare } from '../data/pricing';

const pct = `${amcShare.low * 100}–${amcShare.high * 100}%`;
---

<Base
  title={`Service & AMC — ${site.name}`}
  description="What the warranty covers, what the annual service plan covers, and what it costs. Written down before you need it."
  waContext="the service plan"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="brass-rule"></div>
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:16px">Service</p>
      <h1 class="dsp" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5.4vw,4rem)">
        What happens<br />when something<br />stops working
      </h1>
      <div class="measure" style="margin-top:22px">
        <p class="lede">
          A smart home does not fail all at once. It drifts — a firmware update
          changes an app, a battery dies, an ISP swaps your router and half the
          house forgets its own name. This page is what we do about that.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="measure">
        <p
          class="accent-line"
          style="font-size:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2.1rem);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding-top:24px"
        >
          The second year is when you find out who installed your house.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:34px">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Included · first year</span>
          <h3 class="dsp">Warranty</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Manufacturer warranty on every device, handled by us — you never chase a brand</li>
            <li>Faulty hardware replaced, labour included</li>
            <li>Scene and automation changes, remotely, at no charge</li>
            <li>Help when your router or internet provider changes</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="price">Included in every install</span>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Optional · year two onward</span>
          <h3 class="dsp">Annual service plan</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A preventive visit once a year — firmware, batteries, network health</li>
            <li>Remote monitoring, so we usually see a fault before you do</li>
            <li>Priority call-outs with a response time in writing</li>
            <li>Unlimited scene changes and re-configuration</li>
            <li>Labour on out-of-warranty repairs</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="price">{pct} of installed value per year</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="small measure" style="margin-top:16px">
        The {pct} figure is the industry benchmark for integrator service
        contracts, and it is what we price against. Your exact number is on your
        handover sheet. TODO: confirm the client's actual AMC pricing and
        response-time commitments before launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sechead"><h2 class="dsp">The honest bits</h2></div>
      <div class="worries" style="margin-top:26px">
        <div class="worry">
          <h3>Do I have to take the plan?</h3>
          <p>
            No. Plenty of homes run for years without one and just call us when
            something breaks, paid per visit. The plan is worth it if you have
            curtains, locks or more than about twenty devices — those are the
            things with batteries and moving parts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="worry">
          <h3>What if a brand discontinues my device?</h3>
          <p>
            It happens, and standards-based hardware is our main defence — a
            Matter device keeps working with your hub even if its own app is
            retired. Where something genuinely cannot be saved, the plan covers
            the labour to swap it; you pay for the replacement device.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="worry">
          <h3>How fast do you actually turn up?</h3>
          <p>
            TODO — put the real committed response time here, split by "house is
            usable" and "house is not". A specific number is worth more than the
            word "prompt", which every competitor uses and nobody believes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="worry">
          <h3>What if I move house?</h3>
          <p>
            The plan moves with you, and we will help the new owners take over the
            system rather than leaving them with a house full of devices and no
            logins. Handing over cleanly is part of the job.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stack g16 measure">
        <div class="brass-rule"></div>
        <h2 class="dsp">Already have a system?</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          We take on homes somebody else installed. Send us a list of what you
          have and we will tell you what can be rescued, consolidated, or needs
          replacing — before quoting anything.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px">
          <a class="btn btn--wa" href={whatsappLink('taking over an existing system')} rel="noopener">
            Send us your kit list
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
